{"id": 3, "ts": 1780576746.9048455, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019d like to start by putting Candidate\u202fB forward as the provisional choice.\u202fTheir very conscientious nature speaks directly to operational reliability, and their proven ability to handle stress well aligns with the stress\u2011resilience we need for long\u2011distance flights.\u202fIn addition, their skill in assessing weather conditions and excellent computer abilities demonstrate solid technical and cognitive competence for complex, international operations.\u202fWhile I acknowledge the feedback that they can come across as pretentious and sometimes adopt the wrong tone, these communication style issues are less critical than the core safety\u2011related strengths they exhibit, especially when compared with the other candidates who have more pronounced gaps (e.g., Candidate\u202fC\u2019s poor willingness to develop, Candidate\u202fD\u2019s moodiness and isolation, Candidate\u202fA\u2019s unfriendly demeanor).\u202fTherefore, I recommend we consider Candidate\u202fB as the leading option, while remaining mindful of the need to address their communication style during onboarding."}
