{"id": 11, "ts": 1780576842.0337443, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I\u2019m leaning toward Candidate\u202fC as the best overall fit. While Sarah highlighted Candidate\u202fB\u2019s strong technical competence and stress resilience, the note that B has a weak memory for numbers raises a concrete attention\u2011and\u2011information\u2011accuracy risk on long\u2011distance flights. Moreover, B\u2019s \u201cnasty remarks\u201d and grumpy demeanor could undermine the crew\u2011cooperation that Sarah rightly flags as critical. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC is described as \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis,\u201d \u201cmakes correct decisions quickly,\u201d and is \u201cregarded as 100\u202f% reliable,\u201d all of which directly support operational reliability, stress resilience, and decision quality. The fact that C \u201ccreates a positive crew atmosphere\u201d addresses the crew\u2011cooperation concern more robustly than B\u2019s technical strengths can compensate. Although C has communication difficulties and is not eager for further education, the immediate safety\u2011critical criteria\u2014reliability, calmness under pressure, and crew harmony\u2014appear stronger in C than B\u2019s technical edge. Therefore, I recommend moving forward with Candidate\u202fC."}
