{"id": 29, "ts": 1780576931.8061106, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I\u2019m leaning toward Candidate\u202fC as the strongest overall fit. The new input from James confirms that C \u201cunderstands complicated technology,\u201d giving us solid evidence of technical and cognitive competence\u2014an essential safety\u2011critical requirement. Combined with the earlier points that C is 100\u202f% reliable, stays calm in a crisis, and makes correct decisions quickly, his profile now covers reliability, stress resilience, decision quality, and technical ability.\nWhile we still have concerns about C\u2019s egocentric style and communication difficulty, James reports no concrete incidents showing these traits harming crew cooperation. In contrast, we still lack any concrete evidence of Candidate\u202fB\u2019s decision\u2011making quality under pressure or his adaptability, despite his strong stress handling and conscientiousness. Given the current evidence, C\u2019s strengths are better substantiated across the core pilot criteria, and the weaknesses are less proven.\nTherefore, I would provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fC, pending any further data on A or D that might shift the balance."}
