{"id": 44, "ts": 1780577015.10497, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fC is the strongest overall fit.\u202fWhile Emily confirmed we have no concrete evidence that Candidate\u202fB\u2019s weak memory for numbers has ever translated into a safety\u2011critical error, we do have a clear, documented concern: B \u201cmakes nasty remarks about his colleagues,\u201d which directly threatens crew cooperation and professional communication\u2014key safety criteria for long\u2011distance operations. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC\u2019s egocentric style and difficulty communicating ideas have not been shown to impair crew dynamics; the panel has only speculative concerns about his willingness to pursue further education. Given that B\u2019s memory limitation is unproven but his interpersonal behavior is a proven risk, C\u2019s proven reliability, calmness in crisis, rapid correct decision\u2011making, and technical competence still outweigh the unresolved issues.\nTherefore, I keep my vote for Candidate\u202fC."}
